    "claims": [
      {
        "source": "docs/03b-weighted-threefolds.md#3b10-sextics-with-a-binary-summand",
        "pr": 264,
        "statement": "For a smooth sextic fourfold F=H(x0,x1,x2,x3)+B(s,t) in some linear coordinates, the negative eigenspace of the binary sign is in N^1 H^4. If F is invariant under an involution of signature (3,3), its entire invariant H^4 is in N^1.",
        "hypotheses": "Smooth degree-six hypersurface and an additive 4+2 splitting. The original splitting may be in arbitrary linear coordinates. The second assertion additionally requires the stated (3,3) involution.",
        "consequence": "The source obtains certificates for every odd numerator at every positive pole order for an even sextic with a binary summand, using prior support-to-certificate, higher-pole and coefficient-descent results.",
        "argument_reported": "Order-three quotient for one binary-sign-negative character, cubic and quintic Wronskian spans and finite Fano maps for the other two. A commuting-projection argument chooses a splitting stable under the involution.",
        "change": "Generalizes the earlier mixed-parity, separately-even binary example of the two-reflection theorem; the prior example is absorbed into this result.",
        "dimensions": "Chapter 4 adds projective equation-locus dimension 60 and quotient dimension 43. Its mixed-parity stratum has projective dimension 55 and lies in the two-reflection family.",
        "attribution": "PR and source commit by benediamond, prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance according to the PR."
      },
      {
        "source": "docs/04-known-locus-and-frontier.md#strict-growth-and-sectors",
        "pr": 265,
        "statement": "A strict Hall condition on the monomial Higgs graph gives strict dimension growth for images of proper nonzero subspaces. Under the sector hypotheses, every real sub-variation after a dominant smooth connected base change is zero or the whole sector.",
        "hypotheses": "Finite diagonal group fixing the Fermat sextic in P^5 or P(1,1,1,1,2), real character chi with values ±1 and chi different from the determinant character delta. Equal upper/lower dimensions, strict Hall graph condition, plus two-step Higgs products and surjectivity/no-common-kernel monomial conditions for the middle piece on fourfolds.",
        "support_corollary": "Requires a finite-type G-stable family of divisor supports dominating the entire invariant coefficient family, whose Gysin image contains a nonzero class in the sector at the geometric generic point.",
        "change": "The first four table rows recover earlier alternatives. New criterion rows are the fully paired-sign invariant residual sector (58,230,58) and the paired-sign negative/positive sectors (100,424,100)/(108,442,108). Each needs the supporting-family input.",
        "attribution": "PR authored/merged by benediamond, source commit by Claude. PR and source commit expressly credit fqlx for the strict-growth argument and odd-cycle certificate from the research notes of PR 245. The PR generalizes to matching/connectivity and the fourfold conditions.",
        "computation_status": "The embedded monomial script and its reported checks were inspected as source and were not run by Hodge Lab."
      },
      {
        "source": "docs/03d-hodge-loci.md#3d7-the-criterion-from-weight-one",
        "pr": 266,
        "statement": "Re-proves the moving-class criterion and the existing order-three weighted-threefold theorem of section 3D.4 using Betti/de Rham conjugation, positivity on H^1 of curves, and strict growth of the Higgs maps.",
        "hypotheses": "Smooth irreducible family of invariant threefold equations with delta different from 1. Retains a seed with surjective Noether–Lefschetz map and a kernel direction pairing nontrivially with the specified residue class. Replaces the scalar-commutant condition by strict growth at one member. The weight-one alternative applies to images of relative curve correspondences over a smooth connected dominant base change.",
        "conclusions": "A nonzero such correspondence surjects onto the invariant sector. The filtration decomposition and invertibility of the correspondence composed with its transpose follow. Coherent deformation of line bundles and fiber integration supply the moving family and trace interpretation.",
        "scope_limits": "The extension covers real ±1 characters chi different from delta. It excludes the combined nontrivial complex eigensector of section 3D.6, whose individual upper/lower dimensions differ. It does not directly supply the corresponding fourfold argument. Standard conjugation, horizontality and trace compatibilities remain stated inputs.",
        "change": "Alternative proof of existing support claims. The section 3D.4 result used by the older cycle-q2 route retains its prior statement; no additional exact-target primitive or accepted solve is supplied.",
        "attribution": "PR authored/merged by benediamond, source commit by Claude. The PR credits fqlx for strict growth."
      }
    ],
