    "reported_claims": {
      "reported_degree_six_reduction": "For four-plus-two-residual at q=1 and A=X0^3 Y0^3, benediamond reports every legal degree-six denominator can be written D=D_c(x)+lambda F, with nonzero [D_c] in the 33-dimensional kernel of multiplication by A in core Jacobian degree six. The restriction includes complex denominators of arbitrary parity.",
      "reported_equivalence": "The post reports equivalence of a degree-six certificate to a core sextic D_c and degree-seven polynomial core field p satisfying p(H)=A D_c and D_c div(p)=p(D_c). Their rational field p/D_c is divergence-free. Existence for the prescribed source remains open.",
      "reported_computation_scope": "The author cites maximal Jacobian multiplication ranks and two Hessian systems modulo scalar matrices at p=101 with affine quotient lengths 8 and 257, plus good complete-intersection reduction. These support the stated characteristic-zero reduction in the post. No calculation was replayed by this monitor.",
      "reported_shared_denominator_obstruction": "The post also reports that one sextic denominator cannot serve every odd sextic source, using a Fermat reduction modulo five and joint injectivity. This claim concerns a shared denominator across sources.",
      "reported_prym_result": "For C: w^3=f(t^2) mapping to E: w^3=f(v), the anti-invariant target differential dt/w lies in the three-dimensional Prym. The author reports absolute simplicity and geometric rational endomorphism algebra Q(sqrt(-3)), based on Frobenius/root-ratio calculations at 31 and 13. The post concludes the differential cannot come from an elliptic quotient of this Prym.",
      "prior_context": "The post explicitly sharpens kejace’s degree-at-most-five exclusion. It identifies the new open core condition with the m=0 degree-six family left unresolved by kmehltretter82’s bounded checks and links DiamondJM’s core equation. Divisor support was already attributed to the book’s two-reflection theorem. The new comment supplies an attributed reduction and geometric obstruction while the explicit degree-six pair remains open.",
